\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Share of heads where allocation beats the best corner by $\geq 2\times $, versus context (colours as Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:teaser}b). Every model decays, at $-1.4$ to $-14.6$ points per doubling; the circled point was held out. \textbf  {(b)} The linearized cost model's predicted gain over uniform divided by the exactly recomputed gain: all 24 configurations fall within $[0.79,1.34]$, while the measured gains themselves span $20$--$37\times $. \textbf  {(c)} \emph  {Projected, not measured} ({\color  {tbdcol}\textbf  {TBD}\nobreakspace  {}[R8]}): the hypothesis the router experiment tests. Always-allocate wins at low $D_2$ and always-evict at high $D_2$; a per-head router should track the upper envelope, with the largest margin in the mixed middle.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{2}{3}{\textbf {(a)} Share of heads where allocation beats the best corner by $\geq 2\times $, versus context (colours as Fig.~\ref {fig:teaser}b). Every model decays, at $-1.4$ to $-14.6$ points per doubling; the circled point was held out. \textbf {(b)} The linearized cost model's predicted gain over uniform divided by the exactly recomputed gain: all 24 configurations fall within $[0.79,1.34]$, while the measured gains themselves span $20$--$37\times $. \textbf {(c)} \emph {Projected, not measured} (\tbd {[R8]}): the hypothesis the router experiment tests. Always-allocate wins at low $D_2$ and always-evict at high $D_2$; a per-head router should track the upper envelope, with the largest margin in the mixed middle}{figure.2}{}}
